                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.8212a/3: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Liberia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Walton</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Monrovia</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1939-05-24T12:00:00-00:44">May 24, 1939—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received
                        1:40 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>35. Reference Department’s instruction No. 124 of March 7th subject conciliation
                    convention. Liberian Government desires to know if expense of the Permanent
                    Commission shall be a continuous charge on the contracting parties or whether
                    those expenses arise only as and when the Commission is called upon to
                    function.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Walton</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
